---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="MCP tool schema size vs strict clients | rea.run"
  description="Huge tools/list payloads and providers with per-schema caps — upgrade and client choices."
  path="/faq/mcp-schema-size/"
>
  <article class="prose-page mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14">
    <p class="text-sm"><a class="quiet-link" href="/faq/">← FAQ hub</a></p>

    <p class="badge badge-accent mt-4">FAQ · P1</p>
    <h1 class="display mt-4 text-4xl text-[var(--color-ink)]">MCP tool schema size vs strict clients</h1>
    <p class="lede mt-4 !max-w-none">When connecting REA makes the entire agent refuse every request.</p>
    <h2>What breaks</h2>
    <p>Some providers enforce a <strong>per-tool JSON schema size cap</strong>. REA’s full <code>tools/list</code> can advertise many detailed tools; a single oversized schema may cause Moonshot/Kimi-class clients to reject the whole session.</p>
    <h2>What to do (operator)</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Upgrade <code>rea-agents</code> — schema compaction and discovery fixes ship over time.</li>
      <li>Prefer clients that tolerate large catalogs, or use CLI for heavy jobs.</li>
      <li>Watch upstream roadmap work on bounded-resource MCP usability; do not “fix” caps by corrupting schemas.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>This is a compatibility problem, not permission to bypass vendor limits with malformed tool descriptors.</p>

    <footer class="mt-12 border-t border-[var(--color-line)] pt-6 text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)] not-prose">
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider">Sources</p>
      <ol class="mt-3 list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5 text-xs">
          <li><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/issues/1484" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Issue #1484 — Moonshot/kimi schema cap</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/issues/1327" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Issue #1327 — npm latest vs main schema fixes</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/issues/1065" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Issue #1065 — MCP usability under bounded resources</a></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="mt-4"><a class="quiet-link" href="/compliance/">Compliance</a></p>
    </footer>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
